WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:03.340
Hey YouTubers, it's Charlie

00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:04.471
So today we're going to talk about

00:00:04.471 --> 00:00:07.293
Game of Thrones characters that just do not give a crap

00:00:07.293 --> 00:00:08.856
about the Iron Throne anymore.

00:00:08.856 --> 00:00:10.008
Chief among them,

00:00:10.008 --> 00:00:13.563
dragons. Obviously dragons absolutely do not care for the Iron Throne.

00:00:13.563 --> 00:00:14.723
Not that they ever did.

00:00:14.723 --> 00:00:17.033
Just, careful for spoilers through season 4

00:00:17.033 --> 00:00:18.993
we don't necessarily have to get in to book stuff, so

00:00:18.993 --> 00:00:21.367
if you only watch the show, you should be just fine.

00:00:21.367 --> 00:00:23.257
If you want to add anybody to the list,

00:00:23.257 --> 00:00:24.950
feel free. This is only going to be a top 5

00:00:24.950 --> 00:00:26.941
So there's no way everyone's going to make the list.

00:00:26.941 --> 00:00:28.593
So here we go, starting with number 5:

00:00:28.822 --> 00:00:29.322
Bronn

00:00:29.322 --> 00:00:30.418
This is almost a cheat,

00:00:30.418 --> 00:00:33.186
because he's like the king of not caring about almost anything.

00:00:33.186 --> 00:00:34.821
I think maybe having sex,

00:00:34.821 --> 00:00:36.127
like, that's probably what he cares about most.

00:00:36.378 --> 00:00:37.178
Having sex,

00:00:37.178 --> 00:00:39.232
and filling his pocket with someone else's gold.

00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:41.705
It seems like he's been Tyrion's best friend,

00:00:41.705 --> 00:00:44.566
but really, I think he's only been his best friend as long as

00:00:44.566 --> 00:00:47.275
Tyrion has supported his request for more gold.

00:00:47.275 --> 00:00:48.733
Bronn's like an afternoon delight,

00:00:48.733 --> 00:00:50.338
love the one you're with kinda person.

00:00:50.338 --> 00:00:51.893
I don't think he's obsessed with money.

00:00:51.893 --> 00:00:53.373
Yes, he's a mercenary,

00:00:53.373 --> 00:00:55.317
he works for whoever pays him,

00:00:55.317 --> 00:00:57.750
but he's not a slave to the acquisition of wealth

00:00:57.750 --> 00:00:58.916
that the Lannisters are.

00:00:58.916 --> 00:01:00.976
I think a really good example of his character is

00:01:01.039 --> 00:01:04.079
the last time he saw Tyrion in The Black Cells.

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:06.713
His friend was getting ready to get his head chopped off,

00:01:06.713 --> 00:01:09.437
and it just seemed like he almost didn't care about anything.

00:01:09.437 --> 00:01:10.953
He was kind of sad to see him go,

00:01:10.953 --> 00:01:12.580
but he was like, "well, what're you going to do?"

00:01:12.580 --> 00:01:14.473
Now that Bronn is a lord though

00:01:14.473 --> 00:01:16.817
I'm interested to see how it changes his behavior

00:01:16.949 --> 00:01:17.749
in season 5.

00:01:17.749 --> 00:01:19.973
The show has actually turned him into a main character,

00:01:19.973 --> 00:01:21.250
like if you look at the season 5

00:01:21.250 --> 00:01:23.208
cast list, he's actually a main character.

00:01:23.208 --> 00:01:24.440
In the books, not so much.

00:01:24.440 --> 00:01:25.773
Moving on to number 4 though:

00:01:25.972 --> 00:01:26.772
Sansa Stark

00:01:26.772 --> 00:01:30.300
This is a pretty easy one, I think she just mostly cares about staying alive

00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:33.714
Little Finger seems like he has this very creepy, grand plan for her.

00:01:33.714 --> 00:01:36.334
She kind of started to pick up on it at the end of season 4,

00:01:36.334 --> 00:01:38.989
like she dyed her hair, they're obviously going to go on the run.

00:01:38.989 --> 00:01:41.233
But I don't think she really cares about

00:01:41.240 --> 00:01:42.794
who sits on the Iron Throne,

00:01:42.940 --> 00:01:44.100
least of all, herself.

00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:46.142
You'd think that the surviving Starks

00:01:46.142 --> 00:01:49.131
would care most about finding the rest of their family.

00:01:49.131 --> 00:01:52.456
Of all them, Sansa's kind of been the slowest to get her ass in gear.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:55.758
That's why in season 5 I'm really excited to see if she does anything crazy!

00:01:55.758 --> 00:01:58.013
Like if she comes to the breaking point, like if Arya

00:01:58.013 --> 00:02:00.887
and Jon Snow are starting to go through big character transformations,

00:02:00.887 --> 00:02:02.549
maybe Sansa's going to as well.

00:02:02.549 --> 00:02:04.448
There's this thing called narrative proximity

00:02:04.448 --> 00:02:06.013
that George R. R. Martin is a big fan of,

00:02:06.013 --> 00:02:08.333
where big things happen to similar characters.

